Z||000000||fiero87||10-10-2000||08:57 PM||||Hello,<P>I have the opertunity to purchase a hardly used 4 sp, with the 4.10 final gear ratio.  Now i know nothing about the logic behind this, but i have heard this is the best transmission for a street, 1/4 mile set up?  What improvements can i expect to see with my basicly stock vehichle?  Is this going to equate into worse gas milage?  Any info is appreicated.  Thanks<P>Tim||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||10-10-2000||09:11 PM||||It means that at 65 mph, you are buzzing along at about 3000 rpms! For me, it means creeping through town in 4th gear without ever having to downshift because the engine is lugging. If you do highway driving, it may not be a good choice. For average highway speeds and driving in town, the only thing better is an automatic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||10-10-2000||11:03 PM||||<BR>the 4:10 = Rock Crusher. mine has 120K miles on it and has never had a problem. It will get you off the line better than any other "stock" trans in a fiero. but you will give up the top end. my little 2m4 tops out at about 100-105 mph (Redline) but I can deal with it because i ONLY get posi never single  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and i'm runnin on 3 cylinders  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||10-11-2000||08:20 AM||||i installed on in my 86 SE V6. it tachs up great and pulls like a train through 3rd! GT Bastard has the car now.. might want to ask him about it... i drove it from Atlanta to South Dakota (1300miles) all highway drivin' and it wasn't as bad as i thought it would be... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-11-2000||08:29 AM||||I drove Ed Parks 85SE with the 4.10 and it was nice.  He said that his hwy mileage was unaffected because the engine is running in it's sweet spot rpm at 70.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||10-11-2000||08:30 PM||||I ran the numbers for you on Dragstrip2000 and if you have the v6 four speed with a stock engine it will run the quarter mile in 15.74 @ 85 mph and 0-60 mph in 8.0 seconds. If you put in the performance four speed transmission (4.10 final drive) that same car would go the quarter mile in 15.72 @ 83.4 mph and 0-60 mph in 7.7 seconds.||||reg||1
